# Composer

The message box at the bottom of the Agent pane: attach, type, send.

- You supply `value`, `onChange`, `onSend`, `onAttach` and optionally `state` (`idle`, `streaming` or `unavailable`), `mode` (`regular` shows "Attach a file", `photo` shows "Photo"), `attachment` (the props of a `ChatAttachment`, shown below the entry), `onStop` and `placeholder`.
- The entry is 50px tall with a 1px `border-subtle` stroke and `radius-small` corners: a `ButtonLink` to attach, the text in `body-small`, then a compact `ButtonPrimary` labelled Send.
- Send is disabled until there is text or an attachment; an attachment alone can be sent. While the Agent is replying the placeholder reads "Agent is responding…" and Send becomes a Stop `ButtonSecondary`.
- Unavailable is different from empty: the entry turns `surface-subtle`, the placeholder reads "Chat is unavailable" and attaching is disabled.
- Focus in the text draws a 2px `border-focus` stroke around the whole entry. Enter sends.
